1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming at the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,760
I kick a pebble and it flies off on a cloud.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,260
Joking around, to the PE teacher Kashiwa,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
I got laughed at for
staying as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow rouse
my spirits somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
There's only winning.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, the unchanging streetscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,900
the sun is already setting.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,180
Yakitori Honbari.

12
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,860
Is there?

13
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:04,060
from the sosui to the vast sky,
the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:12,700
Tomorrow too, it ends in a fall Maybe the magazine again,
happiness, they say.

16
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:16,280
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it by taking the easy way.

17
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:25,980
Ryuichiro Nakagawa

18
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:30,060
Father of Keiichi Nakagawa,
head of the world's largest group company

19
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:31,820
President of Nakagawa Concept

20
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,800
whose catchphrase is
"Can you work 72 hours straight?"

21
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,780
is a super businessman

22
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:42,780
Here it comes! Here it comes!
Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes!

23
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,240
It's not like we have
to buy from your company.

24
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,860
There are plenty of other oil companies,
you know.

25
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,360
Let's wait another 15 seconds.

26
00:01:58,680 --> 00:01:59,400
Understood.

27
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,160
We'll sell at the price you offered.

28
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,160
Thank you.

29
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:06,860
I'll send the detailed
contract from Nakagawa Oil.

30
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:07,620
Well then.

31
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,960
President, you look exhausted.

32
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:16,460
Perhaps you should take a little rest.

33
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:17,180
Uuugh.

34
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,800
We still have 7 minutes until bedtime.

35
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,320
Yes, sir.

36
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,840
Your next schedule is

37
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:27,220
a meeting with Mikimatsu
Nakagawa in 2 minutes.

38
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,320
After that, you'll take a 5-minute nap.

39
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:32,000
The uncle from Hawaii.

40
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:32,660
Yes.

41
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:36,460
Right after you wake up, you have a
video call with the French president.

42
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,400
Then, after arriving at Heathrow Airport,

43
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,720
lunch with the British Chamber of Commerce.

44
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,400
That's enough.

45
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,700
But about the meeting
with Uncle Mikimatsu...

46
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:49,320
We should be over the Atlantic Ocean right now,
shouldn't we?

47
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,280
Hello

48
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:59,460
Hey, open up.

49
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,240
Yes, Ryuichiro.

50
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:07,620
Mr. Mikimatsu, I'm terribly sorry.

51
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,480
He'll be right with you.

52
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,480
No, it's fine.

53
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:15,580
When we set up today,
I meant to show off my girlfriend,

54
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:17,080
but she dumped me.

55
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:20,700
So I don't have any special business.

56
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,700
Just seeing your face after
so long is enough for me.

57
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:25,800
Just let them sleep.

58
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:28,340
Yes, thank you very much.

59
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:31,520
See you again, Yuki!

60
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,000
Oh no! I fell asleep for this long!

61
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,240
What about Uncle Mikimatsu?!

62
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,120
He went home two minutes ago.

63
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,720
What?

64
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:47,140
Me, whose motto is "Can you work 72 hours?"

65
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,460
to make such a blunder...

66
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,920
Nakagawa Family, Oil Sword

67
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:58,740
Quit being a police officer?

68
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,200
What do you mean, Nakagawa?

69
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:05,820
My father suddenly announced he's retiring
as president of the Nakagawa Group,

70
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:09,360
and I've been named his successor.

71
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:13,340
Why would that father, who loves work more
than his three meals a day, do such a thing?

72
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:17,020
My father, whose motto is
"Can you work 72 hours?"

73
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,120
fell asleep at 71 hours and 55 minutes.

74
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,020
My father is strict with others,

75
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:24,980
so he felt he had to be
just as strict with himself.

76
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,000
So he decided to retire.

77
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,700
Just five minutes short.

78
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:33,640
Nakagawa:
So you're really quitting the police force?

79
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:34,600
Yes.

80
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:38,740
I always knew I'd have to follow
in my father's footsteps someday,

81
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,420
but I never expected it to be this soon.

82
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:43,740
I still have a lot of unfinished
business at the police box,

83
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,540
so I'm really torn.

84
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:48,220
Nakagawa,
what nonsense are you talking about?

85
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:53,300
Who in their right mind would turn down the presidency of the Nakagawa Group,
with over 100 trillion yen in assets?

86
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,960
Ryo-chan, do you want Kei-chan to quit?

87
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:59,240
No, I don't want him to quit either.

88
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:02,080
But as a distant relative,

89
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:07,520
I've long believed that Nakagawa is
the rightful heir to the Nakagawa Group.

90
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,840
I became a relative of the Nakagawa family.

91
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,760
Come on, Bucchan.

92
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:17,860
That's the kind of relationship
Nakagawa and I have.

93
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:25,960
The husband of the paternal aunt of my
younger brother Kinjiro's wife's mother,

94
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:29,580
is the son of the daughter of
Uncle Nakagawa's younger brother.

95
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,180
I don't really understand it, but

96
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,260
anyway,

97
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:36,160
I believe Nakagawa is the one
who should lead the Nakagawa Group

98
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:41,780
and is the only man who can
restore the world economy.

99
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:46,100
Senpai, you really think that highly of me?

100
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,220
Of course.

101
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:50,680
If it means making you president,
I'll do anything.

102
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:53,900
That's right, starting today,
I'll be your secretary.

103
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,160
Senpai Nakagawa

104
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:57,660
Or something like that, he says.

105
00:05:57,660 --> 00:06:00,920
Ryo-chan, you're not up to
something weird again, are you?

106
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:01,920
How rude!

107
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:05,560
Whether my eyes look like
they're thinking that kind of thing

108
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:06,980
Take a good look.

109
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,900
Ryo-loss, what about your police work?

110
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,200
Of course, I'll be resigning.

111
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:15,160
Is that really okay with you?

112
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,660
Nakagawa, let's go.

113
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,720
Y-yes.

114
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:25,140
Once I make Nakagawa president,
I'll become vice president.

115
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:32,080
Alright, Nakagawa, let's go. Are you ready?

116
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,360
Y-yes.

117
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:37,580
So you won't reconsider your retirement,
no matter what?

118
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:38,380
Yes.

119
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:42,560
I believe you're the only one who
can lead the massive Nakagawa Group.

120
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:46,300
Once I've said I'm quitting,
a man doesn't take back his word.

121
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:48,740
But Keiichi is still young,

122
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:50,940
he can't possibly handle your job.

123
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,160
That's not true.

124
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,060
So you've come.

125
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:57,000
Keiichi.

126
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,560
It's been a while.

127
00:06:59,060 --> 00:06:59,740
Hey.

128
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,560
Why, it's Ryotsu!

129
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,820
I'm the boss at Keiichi's workplace.

130
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:08,700
No, I've firmly resigned
from the police force.

131
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:10,720
Please.

132
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,640
Go on, go on, go on.

133
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:17,320
From now on,
I'll be serving as Nakagawa's secretary.

134
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,020
What is this
"president's secretary" business?

135
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:22,160
Keiichi hasn't been decided as president yet,
you know.

136
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,040
With all due respect,

137
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:28,660
Nakagawa has already been named successor by the current president,
hasn't he?

138
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,620
Then let me ask you this.

139
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:34,860
Keichi,
can you really handle your father's job?

140
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:35,940
W-well, that's...

141
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:37,440
I can.

142
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:43,360
Then try doing the president's
72-hour grueling schedule.

143
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:48,680
If you can do that, we'll acknowledge
you as president of the Nakagawa Group.

144
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,600
Understood.

145
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:52,800
Senpai, 72 hours is a bit much,
don't you think?

146
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:55,760
What's with the weak attitude?
I'll make it work somehow.

147
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:59,300
Yeah, Keichi, you can do it.
I'm counting on you.

148
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,560
Y-yes!

149
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,212
Wake up, Nakagawa!

150
00:08:04,262 --> 00:08:07,440
Wake up! Do you know what time it is?

151
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:12,690
Senpai? It's still before dawn!

152
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:15,100
Senpai, it's only 5:30!

153
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:17,540
Shut up! Open up already!

154
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:23,220
Senpai, I'm getting dressed right now,
so please wait a moment.

155
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,960
Ugh, just change in the car!

156
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:26,640
W-what?!

157
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:36,080
Good, read this before
we get to the airport.

158
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,320
That much?

159
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:43,040
We've arrived in Washington.
Now it's breakfast with the president.

160
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,040
So we're going to the White House.

161
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:45,500
That's right.

162
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,640
Excuse me.

163
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,960
We've just received word that

164
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:53,120
due to congestion at Washington International Airport,
our landing will be significantly delayed.

165
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,000
What?

166
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:57,980
We'll miss the next meeting in L.A.!

167
00:08:58,640 --> 00:08:59,720
Guess we'll have to use that trick.

168
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:08,860
Senpai, let's just forget about it.

169
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,580
Stop your grumbling and

170
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:15,180
See? You can do it after all.

171
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:15,840
Yes.

172
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,900
Feng shui.

173
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,880
We have to go further over there.

174
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:28,160
Damn, we ended up in the water after all.

175
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,420
Senpai, are you all right?

176
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:04,820
About the plan for the Nakagawa Group to
commercialize the spring water from Rocky National Park,

177
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:08,060
the one about selling it as
delicious Rocky water, right?

178
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:09,580
Of course, yes.

179
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:10,620
Thank you very much.

180
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,720
Well then, let's have breakfast.

181
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,060
Yes.

182
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,760
Wow, that looks delicious.

183
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,140
Nakagawa, that's enough.

184
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:22,360
Look, because of that earlier trouble we're
already more than ten minutes over schedule.

185
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,600
But I haven't even taken a single bite yet!

186
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,560
If you're eating that,
we'll never make the meeting in Los Angeles.

187
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,360
Come on, let's go.

188
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,640
Excuse me.

189
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,840
A super businessman just like Ryuichiro!

190
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:39,960
Thanks, that was a very good deal.

191
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:41,620
Nakagawa, this way!

192
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,105
Senpai,

193
00:10:43,155 --> 00:10:46,480
What's wrong?
Are we going down the emergency exit?

194
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:49,460
No, the next meeting is
in the building next door.

195
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,240
It's faster to go from here.

196
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:54,500
I've rigged a rope for you,
so cross over here.

197
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,960
Wait, we're crossing on a rope?

198
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:59,220
A former police officer like you can do it.

199
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,500
It's so high!

200
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:04,960
You can definitely do it!

201
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,660
It's your lifeline!

202
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:07,820
Are we really doing this?

203
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,040
Alright!

204
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:12,460
Come on, go!

205
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,160
I should have become a firefighter!

206
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:24,460
Alright, that went well too.
Now, next stop: Japan!

207
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:31,140
We're done! Nakagawa, food!
We're eating in three minutes!

208
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,080
Hey, hold on, I'll do this for you.

209
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,840
It's Nakagawa's signature.

210
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,500
Signature.

211
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:07,720
That's right, you sign the contract.

212
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,900
Excuse me a moment.

213
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:11,380
Here, look, sign it.

214
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:13,380
Signature.

215
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:14,920
Yeah, right there.

216
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:16,780
Good.

217
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,560
That's it, all set.

218
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,280
Just deliver the million tons first, okay?

219
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,180
Now back to the helicopter,
next stop is China.

220
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,400
Xièxie

221
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,360
Good, the contract's done. Next stop, Kenya!

222
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,780
Are we still going?

223
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:30,840
Of course. What's wrong with you,
getting worn out over this much?

224
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,760
You'll never become leader of
the Nakagawa Group at this rate.

225
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,980
Senpai, I'm finished.

226
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:43,060
Good. Get on the helicopter first.

227
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:49,800
Nakagawa, we're returning to
headquarters for a progress report.

228
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:52,060
Hey, Nakagawa, don't fall asleep!

229
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:53,820
Right, the signature, correct?

230
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:56,940
Pull yourself together!
It's only been 50 hours!

231
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:06,060
We're here. Sleep until we reach
the Nakagawa conference room.

232
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,580
I'll take you there myself.

233
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:08,340
That's enough.

234
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:11,820
Looks like Keiichi-kun still isn't up to it.

235
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:15,480
If that's the case, let's gather the
heads of every Nakagawa Group company

236
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,680
and decide on a successor.

237
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,580
Let's hold the meeting in Tokyo.

238
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:23,220
Let's list a few candidates.

239
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,060
Wait a moment, please.

240
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:29,660
Don't give up on him.
Give Nakagawa one more chance.

241
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:30,800
But...

242
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,740
Couldn't he at least be
one of the candidates?

243
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:34,300
Yeah.

244
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:35,820
Alright.

245
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,160
I won't fail next time, I swear.

246
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:43,240
What do you mean the runway can't be used?

247
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,240
That's absurd!

248
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,260
I'm terribly sorry.

249
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,880
The airport has been
reserved for the entire day,

250
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,580
Don't talk nonsense, young man.

251
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,020
It's impossible to
reserve an entire airport.

252
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:55,400
Hurry up and prepare a special plane.

253
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:59,500
The Nakagawa Group has booked
an enormous amount of space,

254
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,940
W-what? The Nakagawa Group?

255
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:03,420
Yes, just look over there.

256
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,620
They've been arriving one
after another since morning.

257
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,000
So this is the famous luxury liner,
the Queen Elizabeth 2?

258
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,340
It really is huge.

259
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,540
Back in Japan after twenty years

260
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:38,020
Now then, shall we begin the meeting
to choose Ryuichiro's successor?

261
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,640
Personally,
I thought Keiichi would be the best choice.

262
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:46,300
Looks like he's still just
a weakling and a loser.

263
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:49,100
After discussing it among
everyone gathered here,

264
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,020
five people have been chosen as candidates.

265
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:57,840
Eiichi, introduce yourself first.

266
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:01,040
I'm Eiichi Nakagawa,
managing director of Nakagawa Products.

267
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:03,260
I'm in charge of futures trading.

268
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:08,840
I'm Juichi Nakagawa,
deputy president of Nakagawa Bank.

269
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:14,180
I also serve as a director of Nakagawa
Airlines and Nakagawa Securities.

270
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:15,640
I'm Baron Nakagawa.

271
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:24,920
Hi, I'm Tsurumatsu, grandson of Grandpa Mikimatsu, and I'm off having fun in Hawaii.
Nice to meet you, aloha way!

272
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,740
Go for it, Tsurumatsu!

273
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:33,480
I work as a local civil servant in Tokyo.
I'm Keiichi Nakagawa. Nice to meet you.

274
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,120
Go for it, Nakagawa!

275
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:40,680
Ryuichiro, we're choosing from these five,
but how should we decide?

276
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:43,140
Could you leave it to me?

277
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:45,260
What do you all think?

278
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:53,460
As president, I must pursue profits
for the employees and their families.

279
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:57,260
So each of these five will
be given 10 billion yen.

280
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:58,860
10 billion yen.

281
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:02,580
Within one day, you'll compete to see
how much you can grow that 10 billion yen.

282
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:04,740
The methods are up to each of you.

283
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:05,740
Understood.

284
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,720
I'll give it my all.

285
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:10,100
I'll double it to 20 billion.

286
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,500
Aloha way!

287
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:14,180
I'll do my best.

288
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,520
Chinese-made adhesive
patches dropped five dollars.

289
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:21,220
Buy!

290
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,000
North Sea crude oil has started moving.

291
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,780
Right, now's the time to sell.

292
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,120
The euro's exchange rate against
the dollar has started climbing.

293
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,240
Just buy about 10 million
euros' worth for now.

294
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,340
Hit it big again!

295
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,600
It just keeps growing.

296
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:42,620
Aloha-oe!

297
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:51,420
Alright, I'm buying five billion yen of Lustack's over-the-counter IT stocks,
even at a loss!

298
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,820
Alright, bail out!

299
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,060
Keep it there, keep it there!

300
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,180
Samba, samba, run away!

301
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,200
We lost again, and we put a billion on it!

302
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:10,320
Senpai, we're already down 9.9 billion!
What do we do?

303
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:11,940
There's still the final race.

304
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:14,060
If it's come to this,
we're going for a super long shot!

305
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:16,720
Nakagawa, it's all or nothing at 181 points!

306
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,200
Buy 100 million worth!
It'll pay over 200 times!

307
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:22,420
Are you sure it's alright
to bet on such a long shot?

308
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,740
It's fine.

309
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:26,760
Leave it to Kankichi Ryotsu,
the man who's strong in a pinch.

310
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:28,860
Yes, understood. Please proceed.

311
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,720
Now, the results.

312
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:37,340
First place: Tsurumatsu, 35 billion yen.

313
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:40,500
Second place: Eiichi-kun, 31.2 billion yen.

314
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:43,940
Third place: Baron-kun, 25 billion yen.

315
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:48,700
Fourth place: Keiichi. And the candidate
in fifth place is eliminated here.

316
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:51,760
Fourth place is Keiichi, 20 billion yen.

317
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:54,640
Juichi-kun has 19.9 billion yen.

318
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,220
Only a 100 million yen difference?

319
00:17:56,220 --> 00:18:00,860
Therefore, Juichi-kun is disqualified. The next round
will be held at the head office building in Tokyo.

320
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:06,580
Please, go ahead.

321
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:12,680
Forget about work, Mr. President,
and let's have some fun with me.

322
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,180
Excuse me, please get off.

323
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:19,000
A president must not be swayed
by the charms of his secretary.

324
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:21,180
Nakagawa,
I won't fall for something like that.

325
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,520
Please, go ahead.

326
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:28,960
Mr. President, please buy me a fur coat.

327
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,260
Okay, let's go, let's go.

328
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,480
Honestly, that idiot.

329
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:37,560
As expected,
he's really the grandson of Mikimatsu.

330
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:40,840
Since Lord Tsurumatsu has taken the
beautiful mistress out for himself,

331
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,460
we can no longer test the next candidate.

332
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:47,400
It can't be helped. Tsurumatsu is disqualified,
so on to the next one.

333
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:51,760
Ready... set...

334
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:05,700
The head of the Nakagawa Group,
whose schedule is measured in minutes,

335
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:08,040
standing soba is an essential.

336
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:11,440
Drink up every last drop of
the broth without spilling it!

337
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:18,760
I'm just a passing mole.

338
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,500
Eiichi, what are you doing?

339
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,900
Eiichi is disqualified.

340
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:28,340
Baron and Keiichi will
take on the final challenge.

341
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:30,900
A company president must
overcome any hardship

342
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:36,900
so the next battle will be Everest.

343
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:44,960
They're pulling further and further ahead.

344
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:49,340
Yes, Everest is certainly
the top of the world,

345
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:54,020
but Tsurumatsu, raised in Hawaii, would
have given up before even starting the climb.

346
00:19:55,060 --> 00:20:00,440
Compared to that, my son climbed Everest
once with the mountaineering club in college.

347
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,000
Shouldn't we have given them a handicap?

348
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,160
Whoever reaches the summit by 5 p.m.

349
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:07,600
will be declared the winner.

350
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:14,180
I'm just a passing Everest mole.

351
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:21,940
Rolling this stone...

352
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,460
No, no, no.

353
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:28,360
What?

354
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:39,140
Baron

355
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:42,000
I think I also heard my senior's voice.

356
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,040
It stopped.

357
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:51,600
Baron

358
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:53,880
Only three minutes left!

359
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,700
Is that the summit over there?

360
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,960
Two minutes left.

361
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,720
Two minutes

362
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,540
Nakagawa, hang in there!

363
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:10,740
Just a little more!

364
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:11,840
Who's there?

365
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,500
It's the Everest mole.

366
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,960
One minute left.

367
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,060
Thirty seconds left.

368
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,640
Nakagawa, hang in there!

369
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:31,520
Senpai?

370
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:34,200
Just 10 meters left!
Give it everything you've got!

371
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,300
Yes.

372
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:37,600
10 seconds left.

373
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,260
5 seconds left.

374
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,420
4 seconds.

375
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:43,440
3 seconds.

376
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,500
2 seconds.

377
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,520
1 second.

378
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,480
Goal, right at 5 o'clock!

379
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,980
We did it, Nakagawa!

380
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:52,880
Senpai.

381
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:53,600
Well done.

382
00:21:54,900 --> 00:21:58,200
Then I'm the vice president.

383
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:03,540
It was a skull. Movable property.

384
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:16,420
Sorry to say, after all that climbing, but my watch turned out to be five minutes slow.
That means I've been working exactly 72 hours.

385
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:20,000
Therefore, I retract my declaration
of retirement as president.

386
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,720
In that case,
what's going to happen to Nakagawa?

387
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:26,980
You may continue on as a police officer.

388
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:28,220
Don't be ridiculous!

389
00:22:28,220 --> 00:22:31,200
All my hard work up to
now has gone down the drain!

390
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,720
What are you going to do about it?

391
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:37,160
Sorry, but I have business to attend to,
so I'll be taking my leave.

392
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:41,960
Eiichi, let's meet again in a few years.

393
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:44,460
All the way here.

394
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,820
That's just like Dad.

395
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:51,980
But this means I can keep
being a police officer!

396
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,400
Nakagawa, you came back after all?

397
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:01,620
Yes, I look forward to
working with you again.

398
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:03,940
By the way, where's Ryo-chan?

399
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:05,600
Right here.

400
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,460
Who's there?

401
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:10,480
It's me again, it's me!

402
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,920
Well, well, look who it is.

403
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:17,440
So you're Mr. Ryotsu,
Nakagawa's distant relative?

404
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:19,240
What brings you here?

405
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:24,080
So, I was thinking,
could I return to being a police officer?

406
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:26,060
That's what I was thinking, anyway.

407
00:23:28,060 --> 00:23:30,140
You no longer have a desk here.

408
00:23:30,140 --> 00:23:33,780
Nakagawa, you can use that desk every day.

409
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:35,400
Y-yes.

410
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,700
Chief, please, have mercy.

411
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:40,040
Idiot!

412
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:43,820
If you're so eager to come back,
work there for a while.

413
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:44,260
But that's...

414
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:57,860
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out to me

415
00:23:59,220 --> 00:24:01,900
I walked on, looking back

416
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,500
Holding Gā-chan's hand

417
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,680
The feeling I had back then

418
00:24:08,620 --> 00:24:11,540
was a strange, mysterious feeling

419
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:16,900
So I walked along the arcade guide tiles

420
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,660
stepping only on the black parts

421
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:28,840
Everyone was a child once,

422
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:30,960
but everyone has forgotten

423
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:34,980
Politicians with their self-important faces

424
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,300
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

425
00:24:38,300 --> 00:24:41,280
Try turning the corner

426
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,860
at that corner

427
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:49,040
and you can meet everyone, everyone

428
00:24:51,180 --> 00:24:53,840
Over there is Kameari

429
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:57,220
Surely it's Kameari

430
00:24:58,460 --> 00:25:02,180
Everyone, come on over to our town!

431
00:25:04,980 --> 00:25:10,180
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari.

432
00:25:11,700 --> 00:25:15,400
Come on, everyone, to our town!

433
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:16,940
Thank you.

434
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:22,720
Whoa, damn,
I got caught by the shopping arcade crowd!

435
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,680
Forcing me into a part-time
job to make me pay off my debts?

436
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:28,880
What a terrible scheme they've come up with.

437
00:25:28,880 --> 00:25:32,600
And why on earth is
Shiratori my part-time partner?

438
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:35,300
Next time: Ryotsu vs. Shiratori!

439
00:25:35,300 --> 00:25:36,840
Part-Time Job Rampage!

440
00:25:36,840 --> 00:25:37,880
Nice to work with you.

441
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:40,800
Over there is Kameari.

442
00:25:41,740 --> 00:25:45,060
Surely Kameari.

443
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:49,200
Come on, everyone, to our town!

444
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:50,800
Thank you.

